  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Changes since 1.1.72:\n- A url() is written to the CSS as it is in the Sass, as other Sass compilers do. The relative urls that the compiler rewrote came out broken (no closing parenthesis, no quotes or query, one folder short), in compressed CSS for almost every relative url.\n- New: \"rewriteUrls\": true, in sassconfig.json or its defaults, reads relative urls as relative to the Sass file and rewrites them correctly for the CSS file.\n- The paths of sassconfig.json, also loadPaths, are relative to its folder, whatever the current directory is. DartSass found no relative load path in the second project that a build compiled.\n- A change to sassconfig.json or its defaults compiles the files again, so a changed option takes effect.\n- A partial imported through loadPaths is a dependency: a change to it compiles the files that import it.\n- Each project has its own dependencies, so a changed partial in a second project of a build is noticed.\n- An import added to or removed from a partial counts at once, also in a long Visual Studio session or a build process that is kept between builds.\n- Abstractions.Sass.CIBuild depends on no package: it no longer brings DartSassHost into the projects that use it.\n- An unchanged source map is no longer written on every compile.",
